pw-proof: why PW-Lock is refused. PW-Lock 0x58c5f491aba6d61678b7cf7edf4910b1f5e00ec0cde2f42e0abb4fd9aff25a63 (type), args 0x4203673aaee9eab3528763c49c963cfab09e44f4
  a 61 CKB cell under PW-Lock: https://testnet.explorer.nervos.org/transaction/0xdc7854e3c8a1357b27bd43ca60ef59cadf2c8b1ef32d884686fcaed43633167b
  spend: inputs 2 (PW-Lock at 1), witnesses 1: the PW-Lock input has no witness, no signature
  accepted with no signature, PW-Lock cell 61 → 62 CKB: https://testnet.explorer.nervos.org/transaction/0x36410febd935b570377806b9605cb3bf90ac56c02f8e3cdf58ec4208d1f5bcc8
  committed: an input under PW-Lock needs nobody's signature, so a stranger could add one to any
  transaction and get the session lock's owner mode. Hence "owner-lock-unsafe", opt-in or not.

